    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n11935" root="دأل" body-key="d">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">دَؤُولٌ</span></b>  [<i>That runs in the manner termed</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">دَأَلَانٌ</span>,
inf. n. of 1,] is [an epithet] from <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">الدالان</span> [i. e.
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">الدَّأَلَانُ</span>], which signifies <i>a kind of running,</i> as
also ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">دَأالين</span></b>  and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">دااليل</span></b>  [i. e. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">دَآلِينُ</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">دَآليلُ</span>,
pls. of <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">دَأَلَانٌ</span>; the latter irreg., like <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ذَآلِيلُ</span> pl. of
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">دَأَلَانٌ</span>, q. v.]. (Ham p. 458.) [See also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ذَؤُولٌ</span>.]

